#!/usr/bin/env python3
# The proton pack's tests: what the gate runs beside yardr pack check. Needs no
# network and no secret, done in seconds, and never touches a live Bridge: the
# Bridge here is testdata/bridge_stub.py, a socket loop in this process that
# answers the commands proton-imap sends, over STARTTLS with a certificate made
# here and thrown away. Needs openssl and yardr, and fails without them, as
# snowflake's test does: a part that was skipped would leave the pack unpinned.
#
#   functions  proton-imap's own functions called in this process, the
#              cheapest way to hold what needs no server: the query translator
#              as tables of what each q becomes and what it is refused for,
#              the way a search with accents is split into commands, which
#              hosts get no certificate check, the parsers of what imaplib hands
#              back, HTML as text, the bound on an answer, and the program's
#              deadline and timeout.
#   program    proton-imap as a process, run as the yard runs it (parameters on
#              stdin, the login and the base in its environment and nothing
#              else of the yard's) against the stub: each call's answer, in
#              goldens where its shape is the point, then what it does with
#              mail that is big, odd or missing; each way a call fails, with the
#              line it says; and, of every command the stub saw, that all of
#              them were reads, the password never went in the clear and no
#              output held it.
#   exit       this file run again, as a process that dies after its temp dir is
#              made (an openssl that fails ends it at the certificate), to hold
#              that the dir is gone, and as two copies ended by SIGTERM and
#              SIGHUP once their server is up, to hold that no dir and no
#              server is left: cleanup runs at every exit, not only after
#              the last line.
#   yardr      the real yardr in a scratch yard (its own home, an environment
#              of nothing but HOME and PATH, a short path for its socket): the
#              pack applied from its directory, the declaration as the yard reads
#              it, the grants SETUP.md teaches run as written, and the calls made
#              through yardr call against the stub, each held to what the program
#              gives when run on its own.
#
# UPDATE_GOLDEN=1 ./test writes the goldens again from what the program
# prints; read the diff before keeping it.
